      "data": {
        "text": "**Simulating Dead-Lettering**\n\nI'm now focusing on implementing a `dead_letter.py` file to simulate sending failed messages to a dead-letter topic. Even though Google Cloud Pub/Sub has native dead-lettering at the subscription level, I'm opting to demonstrate it by routing failed messages to a separate topic. This approach mirrors a common pattern in handling message processing failures.\n\n\n**Designing Dead-Letter Script**\n\nI'm currently designing the `dead_letter.py` script. The goal is to simulate handling failed messages by publishing them to a dedicated \"dead-letter-topic.\" While Pub/Sub has native dead-lettering, this script will showcase a more general pattern applicable to various message systems and custom dead-letter queue setups. I will assume a message fails, then send it to the dead-letter topic for simplicity.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
